{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdZjzKEE7RTN7dDWhLVJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anthropic's new reporting tools, announced October 28, are built from two sources: internal analytics and employee surveys. With them, a manager can pick a date range and see what a team produced, how much that work cost and where its workflows broke down. The reports also offer recommendations for improving results, and Anthropic is adding pooled group budgets so teams can manage token spending together. TechCrunch describes the release as a clear attempt to demonstrate the return on investment of Anthropic's tools and to show customers how to improve it, which it says is a major concern among large customers.\n\nThe demand for that kind of visibility shows up in a new report from Jellyfish, which makes tools for software developers. Drawing on agentic coding tool usage by 276,000 of its customers, Jellyfish found that spending on these tools has grown 10x since the beginning of the year and now equals about 2% of total engineering cost. Nicholas Arcolano, its chief scientist, told TechCrunch that \"most CFOs didn't plan for\" that growth, and that companies are realizing \"it's not enough to just spend a bunch. You now have to optimize it, make it work.\" TechCrunch also reports that while venture-backed firms are driving token spend, most of the Fortune 500 are not seeing major gains from deploying AI.\n\nAnthropic has strong reasons to supply the answers itself. Claude Code and other tools built on Anthropic models were the most widely used in Jellyfish's data, responsible for nearly a third of all proposed code changes submitted for review. Financials Anthropic shared with investors, as reported by TechCrunch, show 900% net revenue retention, with spending from the same customers in Q3 2026 at nine times its Q3 2025 level. Jellyfish's AI product lead, Nikolas Albarran, noted that the major AI labs are all investing in forward-deployed engineering teams that embed consultants inside customer organizations, and TechCrunch frames these reports as a lighter version of that hands-on help.\n\nBecause the reports combine team analytics with what employees say in surveys, the terms for that data deserve attention. Anthropic says it won't use the data for model training by default. That qualifier means the default setting is the commitment, so a company rolling out the reports would want to confirm how that setting is configured for its own account before employee feedback starts flowing into them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1423,"cache_read_input_tokens":7874,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1423},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca83da92-4f3c-4085-ac30-a0bcdeaf383a","uuid":"63d27ce1-a819-49b8-bd09-f3915be01fc4","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:40:53.044Z","request_id":"req_011CgdZjz56hi9qwS8jhSKHz"}
